<title>RUSSIA: Russian 308-day T-bill yields 27.26 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 308-day T-bill yields 27.26 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 308-day GKO discount Treasury bills was 27.26 percent an an auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the yield would be in the 26.40-27.20 percent range.</p>
<p>Series 23004 bills, maturing on April 8, 1998, the closest maturity date to the new issue, on Tuesday closed at 83.50 to yield 25.67 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow.  </p>
<p>    Series number			    22085</p>
<p>    Issue volume			     6.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)			   8.39 trln</p>
<p>    Bids (cash)				6.80 trln</p>
<p>    Sold					 6.17 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds				   5.02 trln</p>
<p>    Average price			   81.30 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price		 81.17 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield			   27.26 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield		27.49 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor					308 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date			    April 1, 1998</p>
<p>On May 28 the Finance Ministry will offer four trillion roubles of 728-day OFZ interest-bearing bonds (series 24013).</p>
<p>It will also repay 2.96 trillion roubles in a maturing issue of 91-day T-bills (series 21072), pay 210 billion roubles in interest and repay 3.30 trillion roubles on a maturing OFZ interest-bearing bond (series 24004).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
